1245:There are traffic jams all over Champion Street today. I can't even get a cab... Yep, I've got... four cases of tea samples. Magical Dream says that the boss arranged for them last night.
1246:One law of the workplace has become increasingly clear to me recently: No plan can keep up with the boss's whims.
1247:I had been under the impression that these "tea samples" would be no different from the kind you'd find in a shop--a small box containing two to three servings.
1248:But when I arrived at Magical Dream bright and early this morning, I was greeted by four cases more than ten inches thick sit neatly side by side. I realized then just how naive I was to the grueling reality of working life.
1249:Right, I think I understand the situation. Magical Dream isn't terribly far from Bamboo Cloud HQ, at least. I'll have to ask you to walk back.
1250:And so, Yuan Xiao and I are left with no choice but to escort the tea on its journey west to Bamboo Cloud.
1251:You'd better pick up the pace, kind soul! We can still make it before lunch. Otherwise, we'll be stuck waiting in line for roast goose later.
1252:And you could slow down! How are you able to walk so fast while carrying two huge cases of tea?
1253:Well... hehe, I often used to go up the mountain to dig for bamboo shoots, and those were way heavier than tea leaves. Besides, where I come from, even a child could carry these! Why, too heavy for you?
1254:I never said that... Anyway, are you sure your boss didn't stick rocks in these cases? There's no way tea leaves are this heavy. I...
